---
import ExplainerLayout from "../../layouts/ExplainerLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../../components/explainer/Hero.astro";
import Aside from "../../components/explainer/Aside.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/explainer/Figure.astro";
import ControlRange from "../../components/explainer/ControlRange.astro";
import ControlSelect from "../../components/explainer/ControlSelect.astro";
import NextCards from "../../components/explainer/NextCards.astro";
---

<ExplainerLayout title="Interchange Interventions & DAS" breadcrumb="Interchange Interventions" section="interpretability-methods">
<Hero title="Interchange Interventions & DAS" subtitle="Distributed alignment search trains a low-rank interchange that makes a frozen model behave as if one latent variable had been swapped." />

<p>
Activation patching copies a vector at a chosen site. Interchange interventions
make a more targeted claim: there is a subspace whose values act like a specific
causal variable. Distributed alignment search (DAS) trains a rotation, chooses a
low-rank slice of the rotated activation, and swaps only that slice between two
prompts while the model itself stays frozen.
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 1 · Rank-limited interchange against a matched random subspace" canvasId="das-rank-canvas" width="760" height="420" readoutId="das-rank-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="das-rank" label="rank" valueId="das-rank-v" min="1" max="12" step="1" value="4" />
  <ControlSelect id="das-pair" label="latent variable" valueId="das-pair-v" options={[
    { value: "belief", label: "belief space", selected: true },
    { value: "order", label: "adjective order" },
    { value: "binding", label: "binding id" },
  ]} />
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<h2>1. What gets trained</h2>

<p>
DAS does not train the language model. It trains an alignment around one layer:
rotate the activation, expose a small number of rotated coordinates, and optimize
that slice so swapping it transfers the target variable. The downstream model is
then run normally. If the output flips under the learned slice but not under a
random slice of the same rank, the evidence is stronger than plain
decodability.
</p>

<Aside>
  <strong>The random control matters.</strong> A high-dimensional activation has
  many low-rank slices. A learned slice has to beat the chance that any matched
  amount of vector mass would disturb the output.
</Aside>

<h2>2. Floor, ceiling, and transfer index</h2>

<p>
The raw flip rate is hard to read by itself. A corrupted prompt may already flip
some of the time, and even a perfect intervention may not reach 100 percent. The
useful number is normalized between a floor and a ceiling: how much of the
available behavioral transfer did the learned interchange recover?
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 2 · The same efficacy can mean two different claims" canvasId="das-normalization-canvas" width="760" height="320" readoutId="das-normalization-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="das-floor" label="floor" valueId="das-floor-v" min="0" max="0.45" step="0.05" value="0.15" />
  <ControlRange id="das-ceiling" label="ceiling" valueId="das-ceiling-v" min="0.55" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.85" />
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<h2>3. Expressive fit is not yet mechanism</h2>

<p>
A trained alignment can be too expressive. If the aligner finds a subspace that
predictably moves the output but is off the path the model actually uses, it has
shown a useful control surface rather than the internal mechanism. The critique
is not that DAS is invalid; it is that an efficacy number needs supporting
evidence about location, controls, and path specificity.
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 3 · Efficacy without path specificity" canvasId="das-path-canvas" width="760" height="360" readoutId="das-path-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="das-offpath" label="off-pathway leakage" valueId="das-offpath-v" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.35" />
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<p>
The practical reading is conservative. DAS can turn a probe-like readout into a
causal interchange test. It does not, by itself, prove that the model stores the
variable in exactly the learned coordinates or that this is the only path used
for the behavior.
</p>

<div class="source-list">
  <strong>Related pages</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/ml/causal-interventions/">Causal Interventions</a> for ablation, activation patching, and path patching.</li>
    <li><a href="/ml/subspace-geometry/">Subspace Geometry</a> for the rotations and low-rank slices used by DAS.</li>
    <li><a href="/ml/probes-validity/">Probes and Validity</a> for the decodability claim DAS tries to strengthen.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<NextCards cards={[
  { href: "/ml/causal-interventions/", tag: "Before", title: "Causal Interventions", role: "The patching baseline DAS extends." },
  { href: "/ml/subspace-geometry/", tag: "Geometry", title: "Subspace Geometry", role: "Rotations, ranks, and alignment maps." },
]} />

<style>
  .das-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 4.5rem;
    padding: 0.18rem 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const clamp = (x, lo = 0, hi = 1) => Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, x));
    const fmt = (x) => `${Math.round(x * 100)}%`;

    function setupCanvas(id, logicalW, logicalH) {
      const canvas = $(id);
      if (!canvas) return null;
      const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
      const dpr = Math.max(1, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
      const cssW = rect.width || logicalW;
      const cssH = rect.height || logicalH;
      canvas.width = Math.round(cssW * dpr);
      canvas.height = Math.round(cssH * dpr);
      const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
      ctx.setTransform((cssW / logicalW) * dpr, 0, 0, (cssH / logicalH) * dpr, 0, 0);
      return { ctx, w: logicalW, h: logicalH };
    }

    function bar(ctx, x, y, w, h, value, color, label) {
      ctx.fillStyle = "#f6f7fb";
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#d7dde8";
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, 8);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = color;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.roundRect(x, y, w * clamp(value), h, 8);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = "#1f2937";
      ctx.font = "600 13px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText(label, x, y - 8);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#475569";
      ctx.font = "12px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText(fmt(value), x + w + 12, y + h - 8);
    }

    function drawRank() {
      const env = setupCanvas("das-rank-canvas", 760, 420);
      if (!env) return;
      const { ctx } = env;
      const rank = Number($("das-rank")?.value || 4);
      const pair = $("das-pair")?.value || "belief";
      const maxRank = 12;
      const learnedBase = pair === "belief" ? 0.18 : pair === "order" ? 0.1 : 0.14;
      const learned = clamp(learnedBase + 0.72 * (1 - Math.exp(-rank / 3.2)));
      const random = clamp(0.08 + 0.19 * (rank / maxRank) + (pair === "order" ? 0.03 : 0));
      const clean = pair === "belief" ? "Alice believes cup=blue" : pair === "order" ? "big red box" : "pronoun -> source A";
      const source = pair === "belief" ? "Alice believes cup=green" : pair === "order" ? "red big box" : "pronoun -> source B";
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 420);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 19px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("Frozen model, two prompt runs", 36, 40);
      ctx.font = "13px system-ui";
      ctx.fillStyle = "#64748b";
      ctx.fillText("Only the exposed rotated slice is swapped.", 36, 62);

      const boxes = [
        { x: 44, y: 100, label: "base prompt", text: clean, color: "#0ea5e9" },
        { x: 44, y: 222, label: "source prompt", text: source, color: "#f97316" },
      ];
      for (const b of boxes) {
        ctx.fillStyle = "#fff";
        ctx.strokeStyle = "#d7dde8";
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.roundRect(b.x, b.y, 250, 76, 10);
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.fillStyle = b.color;
        ctx.font = "700 12px system-ui";
        ctx.fillText(b.label.toUpperCase(), b.x + 16, b.y + 24);
        ctx.fillStyle = "#111827";
        ctx.font = "600 15px system-ui";
        ctx.fillText(b.text, b.x + 16, b.y + 52);
      }

      ctx.strokeStyle = "#94a3b8";
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.setLineDash([6, 5]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(314, 260);
      ctx.bezierCurveTo(374, 250, 392, 162, 452, 150);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#334155";
      ctx.font = "600 13px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText(`swap rank ${rank} learned slice`, 342, 202);

      for (let i = 0; i < maxRank; i += 1) {
        const x = 448 + i * 15;
        const y = 106;
        ctx.fillStyle = i < rank ? "#be123c" : "#e2e8f0";
        ctx.fillRect(x, y, 10, 110);
      }
      ctx.fillStyle = "#111827";
      ctx.font = "700 14px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("rotated activation", 448, 92);

      bar(ctx, 448, 260, 210, 24, learned, "#be123c", "learned DAS transfer");
      bar(ctx, 448, 330, 210, 24, random, "#94a3b8", "matched random subspace");

      const readout = $("das-rank-readout");
      if (readout) {
        readout.innerHTML = `<span class="das-badge">learned ${fmt(learned)}</span> <span class="das-badge">random ${fmt(random)}</span> Rank ${rank} recovers ${fmt(learned - random)} more target transfer than the matched random control.`;
      }
      $("das-rank-v") && ($("das-rank-v").textContent = String(rank));
      $("das-pair-v") && ($("das-pair-v").textContent = $("das-pair").selectedOptions[0].textContent);
    }

    function drawNorm() {
      const env = setupCanvas("das-normalization-canvas", 760, 320);
      if (!env) return;
      const { ctx } = env;
      const floor = Number($("das-floor")?.value || 0.15);
      const ceiling = Math.max(floor + 0.1, Number($("das-ceiling")?.value || 0.85));
      const raw = clamp(floor + 0.62 * (ceiling - floor));
      const transfer = (raw - floor) / (ceiling - floor);
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 320);
      const x = 78, y = 126, w = 600, h = 38;
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#cbd5e1";
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.fillStyle = "#f8fafc";
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, 12);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.stroke();
      const xf = x + floor * w;
      const xc = x + ceiling * w;
      const xr = x + raw * w;
      ctx.fillStyle = "#fee2e2";
      ctx.fillRect(xf, y, Math.max(1, xc - xf), h);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#be123c";
      ctx.fillRect(xf, y, Math.max(1, xr - xf), h);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 18px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("Normalize the behavioral effect to the available room", 78, 54);
      ctx.font = "12px system-ui";
      ctx.fillStyle = "#475569";
      for (const [label, xx] of [["floor", xf], ["raw", xr], ["ceiling", xc]]) {
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(xx, y - 10);
        ctx.lineTo(xx, y + h + 22);
        ctx.strokeStyle = label === "raw" ? "#be123c" : "#64748b";
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.fillStyle = label === "raw" ? "#be123c" : "#475569";
        ctx.fillText(label, xx - 16, y + h + 40);
      }
      const readout = $("das-normalization-readout");
      if (readout) readout.textContent = `Raw flip rate ${fmt(raw)} becomes transfer index ${fmt(transfer)} after subtracting floor ${fmt(floor)} and ceiling ${fmt(ceiling)}.`;
      $("das-floor-v") && ($("das-floor-v").textContent = fmt(floor));
      $("das-ceiling-v") && ($("das-ceiling-v").textContent = fmt(ceiling));
    }

    function drawPath() {
      const env = setupCanvas("das-path-canvas", 760, 360);
      if (!env) return;
      const { ctx } = env;
      const leak = Number($("das-offpath")?.value || 0.35);
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 360);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 18px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("A strong control surface can bypass the measured mechanism", 44, 42);
      const nodes = [
        { x: 92, y: 170, label: "prompt" },
        { x: 278, y: 104, label: "candidate\nsite" },
        { x: 488, y: 104, label: "target\ncircuit" },
        { x: 650, y: 170, label: "output" },
        { x: 392, y: 246, label: "off-path\nsurface" },
      ];
      function node(n, color) {
        ctx.fillStyle = color;
        ctx.strokeStyle = "#cbd5e1";
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.roundRect(n.x - 54, n.y - 30, 108, 60, 10);
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.fillStyle = "#111827";
        ctx.font = "700 13px system-ui";
        const lines = n.label.split("\n");
        lines.forEach((line, i) => ctx.fillText(line, n.x - 36, n.y - 4 + i * 17));
      }
      function edge(a, b, width, color, dash = false) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = color;
        ctx.lineWidth = width;
        ctx.setLineDash(dash ? [7, 6] : []);
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(a.x + 54, a.y);
        ctx.lineTo(b.x - 54, b.y);
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
      }
      edge(nodes[0], nodes[1], 3, "#64748b");
      edge(nodes[1], nodes[2], 3.5 * (1 - leak) + 1, "#be123c");
      edge(nodes[2], nodes[3], 3, "#64748b");
      edge(nodes[1], nodes[4], 1 + leak * 8, "#f97316", true);
      edge(nodes[4], nodes[3], 1 + leak * 8, "#f97316", true);
      nodes.forEach((n, i) => node(n, i === 4 ? "#fff7ed" : i === 1 ? "#ffe4e6" : "#ffffff"));
      const readout = $("das-path-readout");
      if (readout) readout.textContent = `Off-pathway leakage ${fmt(leak)}: efficacy can stay high while evidence for the named circuit gets weaker.`;
      $("das-offpath-v") && ($("das-offpath-v").textContent = fmt(leak));
    }

    ["das-rank", "das-pair"].forEach((id) => $(id)?.addEventListener("input", drawRank));
    ["das-floor", "das-ceiling"].forEach((id) => $(id)?.addEventListener("input", drawNorm));
    $("das-offpath")?.addEventListener("input", drawPath);
    window.addEventListener("resize", () => { drawRank(); drawNorm(); drawPath(); });
    drawRank();
    drawNorm();
    drawPath();
  })();
</script>
</ExplainerLayout>
